Generalises 7b1e4dd after a valid Codex P1: recomputing only trailing-space
drops at dragend left every other landing spot trusting the preview. Same
defect class as the CI bug, different drop location - a cross-pane drop onto a
tab could silently stay in the source pane when no collision pass ran.

releaseTarget now returns an insertion index counted from neighbours whose
midpoint the pointer has passed. The dragged tab must be excluded in THREE
forms or the index is off by one: [data-dnd-dragging] (the copy tracking the
cursor), [data-dnd-placeholder] (its preview slot), and the original element
still rendered in place when no preview ran. That last one is the subtle case
and only occurs on the broken path. Added data-workspace-tab-id to SortableTab
to make that exclusion by identity rather than by guessing at dnd attributes.

dragover is now purely visual. When a preview did run, the dragend recompute
lands on the same position and movedToPane returns null, so it is a no-op.

Verification worth repeating: disabled handleTabDragOver entirely so no
collision pass could contribute, then ran every drag test. 8 passed, and the
only 2 failures were mid-drag PREVIEW assertions the experiment itself had
disabled (workspace.spec.ts lines 4612 and 6258) - no commit-behaviour test
failed. That is what proves the drop no longer depends on dnd-kit resolving a
target. Check WHICH assertion failed before concluding; a raw pass/fail count
would have looked like a regression here.

